<title>GERMANY: German shipper congress expects 1,400 participants.</title>
<headline>German shipper congress expects 1,400 participants.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 1,400 freight shippers, forwarders and transport suppliers will attend the annual congress of the German shippers association BVL in Berlin from October 23-25, the BVL said.</p>
<p>The main speakers will be Deutsche Lufthansa AG chairman Juergen Weber and Dieter Vogel, chairman of Thyssen AG, the association added.</p>
<p>Subjects under discussion at the meeting in Berlin will include logistics outsourcing, global logistics systems and efficient consumer response models.</p>
<p>Air, sea, road and rail freight operators, forwarders and other transport services suppliers will demonstrate their services at a parallel exhibition.</p>
<p>Contact: BVL, Tel:+49.421.173840, Fax:+49.421.167800</p>
<p>-- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
